    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The datashape is the dataset has 1,000 rows and 7 columns and the data types have numbers, texts, dates. There are no missing values, the sales records run from January 1st/2026 to June 29th 2026. There are 5 branches represented which include Nairobi, Mombasa, Kisumu, Nakuru and Eldoret. The products are Phone, Laptop, Headphones, Tablet and Charger and the sales channels used are In-store, Online and Phone order."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "76BkOVbJcEER"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#total revenue for each order\n",
        "sales[\"revenue\"] = sales[\"quantity\"] * sales[\"unit_price\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "#the month from the order date\n",
        "sales[\"month\"] = sales[\"order_date\"].dt.month_name()\n",
        "\n",
        "#the weekday from the order date\n",
        "sales[\"weekday\"] = sales[\"order_date\"].dt.day_name()\n",
        "\n",
        "#the weekend orders\n",
        "sales[\"is_weekend\"] = sales[\"order_date\"].dt.dayofweek >= 5\n",
        "\n",
        "#products by price\n",
        "def classify_price(price):\n",
        "    if price >= 28000:\n",
        "        return \"Premium\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        return \"Value\"\n",
        "\n",
        "sales[\"price_band\"] = sales[\"unit_price\"].apply(classify_price)\n",
        "\n",
        "sales.head()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
