    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Rank branches by total revenue\n",
        "branch_revenue = sales.groupby(\"branch\")[\"revenue\"].sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Branch ranking by total revenue:\")\n",
        "print(branch_revenue)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Rank branches by number of orders\n",
        "branch_orders = sales.groupby(\"branch\")[\"order_id\"].count().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nBranch ranking by number of orders:\")\n",
        "print(branch_orders)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "J5Hd8xBzh-wc",
        "outputId": "ee6df1b4-99e3-427b-bc59-3ade684df079"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Branch ranking by total revenue:\n",
            "branch\n",
            "Nairobi    26106100\n",
            "Mombasa    14003700\n",
            "Nakuru     11970400\n",
            "Kisumu     10868100\n",
            "Eldoret     8844200\n",
            "Name: revenue, dtype: int64\n",
            "\n",
            "Branch ranking by number of orders:\n",
            "branch\n",
            "Nairobi    376\n",
            "Mombasa    186\n",
            "Nakuru     162\n",
            "Kisumu     159\n",
            "Eldoret    117\n",
            "Name: order_id, dtype: int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Niarobi has the highest order/sales hence the highest revnue and Eldoret has the lowest order/sales hence having the lowerst revnue"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tnMUUo51jFEA"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Top three products by total revenue\n",
        "product_revenue = sales.groupby(\"product\")[\"revenue\"].sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Top three products by revenue:\")\n",
        "print(product_revenue.head(3))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Top three products by units sold\n",
        "product_units = sales.groupby(\"product\")[\"quantity\"].sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nTop three products by units sold:\")\n",
        "print(product_units.head(3))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "cPDTFT3tjWaJ",
        "outputId": "519475e3-4994-4792-bad7-6c6bffeb2e0d"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Top three products by revenue:\n",
            "product\n",
            "Laptop    41535000\n",
            "Tablet    19348000\n",
            "Phone      8880000\n",
            "Name: revenue, dtype: int64\n",
            "\n",
            "Top three products by units sold:\n",
            "product\n",
            "Tablet    691\n",
            "Laptop    639\n",
            "Phone     592\n",
            "Name: quantity, dtype: int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Laptops generated the highest revenue at KES 41,535,000, followed by tablets and phones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Tablets sold the most units 691, while laptops sold 639 units and phones 592\n",
        "\n",
        "The lists are different because laptops are more expensive than tablets, so they generate more revenue even when fewer units are sold."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "g736G6nMj0Qy"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# weekend and weekday orders\n",
        "weekend_sales = sales.groupby(\"is_weekend\").agg(\n",
        "    number_of_orders=(\"order_id\", \"count\"),\n",
        "    total_revenue=(\"revenue\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    average_order_revenue=(\"revenue\", \"mean\")\n",
        "\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "weekend_sales.index = [\"Weekday\", \"Weekend\"]\n",
        "print(weekend_sales)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "5TXbLY2tkiW3",
        "outputId": "ad3549a5-27d9-4903-db21-0fa045b8f570"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "         number_of_orders  total_revenue  average_order_revenue\n",
            "Weekday               723       51856200           71723.651452\n",
            "Weekend               277       19936300           71972.202166\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# the total revenue for each month\n",
        "monthly_revenue = sales.groupby(\"month\")[\"revenue\"].sum().sort_values()\n",
        "\n",
        "# the best and worst months\n",
        "worst_month = monthly_revenue.idxmin()\n",
        "best_month = monthly_revenue.idxmax()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Get their revenue values\n",
        "worst_revenue = monthly_revenue.min()\n",
        "best_revenue = monthly_revenue.max()\n",
        "\n",
        "# the percentage difference\n",
        "percentage_difference = ((best_revenue - worst_revenue) / worst_revenue) * 100\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Worst month:\", worst_month, \"-\", worst_revenue)\n",
        "print(\"Best month:\", best_month, \"-\", best_revenue)\n",
        "print(\"Percentage difference:\", round(percentage_difference, 2), \"%\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "vwdj1jUemAhh",
